# Force LF line endings for text files this pipeline regenerates on every
# automated run, regardless of the committer's local platform/autocrlf
# setting. Without this, a file first committed on Windows (CRLF) and then
# regenerated by GitHub Actions' Linux runner (LF) flips line endings on
# its first automated re-commit -- a real, if harmless, one-time diff-noise
# event this project hit and traced (see the progress log, Step 8). This
# rule prevents it from ever flipping back if the file is later touched
# from a Windows checkout again.
*.csv text eol=lf

# Binary outputs -- never text-normalize these regardless of extension.
*.parquet binary
*.png binary
